# Bulk Operations Test

This test demonstrates Unix-style bulk operations: the `status`, `delete`,
`link`, `unlink`, and `update` commands accept multiple issue IDs as
arguments. Each issue in a batch keeps its per-issue semantics and its own
jj commit; only the output is condensed to one line per changed issue. A
batch with a single issue prints exactly what the per-issue command prints.
Stdin input (the documented `pebbles list | pebbles status in_progress`
composition) is covered by the `bulk-*-stdin` cases next to this file.

## Setup state

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles list
444 [epic] [TODO] Bulk epic (0/0)
333 [des] [TODO] Design task
222 [bug] [TODO] Second bug
111 [bug] [TODO] Login bug

```

## Bulk status update with multiple IDs as arguments

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles status 11111111 22222222 in_progress
✓ Updated 111 [bug] [IN PROGRESS] Login bug
✓ Updated 222 [bug] [IN PROGRESS] Second bug

```

## Bulk all-no-op prints nothing

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles status 11111111 22222222 in_progress

```

## Duplicate IDs collapse to one operation

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles status 22222222 22222222 blocked
✓ Updated issue status
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
Title: Second bug
Type: Bug
Status: BLOCKED

Created: 2026-01-10 12:01:00
Updated: [..]
File: bug-22222222-second-bug.json
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

```

## An unresolvable ID aborts the batch before any change

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles status 11111111 99999999 todo
? failed
Error: No issue found with ID starting with '99999999'

```

## Bulk update with --title

Renaming updates each issue file and the index, one commit per issue.

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles update 11111111 22222222 --title "Renamed in bulk"
✓ Updated 111 [bug] [IN PROGRESS] Renamed in bulk
✓ Updated 222 [bug] [BLOCKED] Renamed in bulk

```

## Bulk link with multiple source IDs

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles link 11111111 22222222 part_of 44444444
✓ Added relationship: 111 part_of 444
✓ Added relationship: 222 part_of 444

```

## Bulk unlink

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles unlink 11111111 22222222 part_of 44444444
✓ Removed relationship: 111 part_of 444
✓ Removed relationship: 222 part_of 444

```

## An unresolvable target aborts the batch

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles link 11111111 part_of 99999999
? failed
Error: No issue found with ID starting with '99999999'

```

## Bulk delete with multiple IDs

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles delete 11111111 22222222
✓ Deleted issue 111
✓ Deleted issue 222

```

## A single argument that is not a status is a missing-status error

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles status 11111111
? failed
Error: Missing status: expected a status (proposed, todo, in_progress, done, blocked) as the last argument. Example: 'pebbles status <id> <status>' or 'pebbles list --status todo | pebbles status in_progress'

```

## Deleting the rest as arguments

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles delete 33333333 44444444
✓ Deleted issue 333
✓ Deleted issue 444

```

## Empty list after deleting everything

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles list
No issues found.

```
